<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lakshmibai</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1828–1858</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Rani Lakshmibai, Rani of Jhansi, Manikarnika</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lakshmibai, the Rani of Jhansi, was the widow of Raja <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gangadhar-rao">Gangadhar Rao</a> and a leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-rebellion-of-1857">Indian Rebellion of 1857</a>. After the British annexed Jhansi she took control of the state during the rising and defended its fort in 1858. She then fought on with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatya-tope">Tatya Tope</a> and was killed in battle near Gwalior in June 1858, becoming a lasting symbol of Indian resistance.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lakshmibai.jpg" alt="Lakshmibai" width="287" height="422" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rani_of_jhansi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
